    "knowledge_point": "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations",
    "problem": "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+5y=9 \\\\ x+0y=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}5y=9 \\\\ x=-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
